elcome Meadow","Windmill Lane","Fresh Water Green","Buttercup Corner","Larkspur Rise","Fresh Water Lane","Promise Rise","Wildflower Gardens","Kindling Rise","Appleseed Grove","Sunrise Acre","Welcome Way","Sunflower Way","Dandelion Grove","Cornflower Way","Seedling Fields","Daybreak Acre","Clover Fields","Morning Lane","Bramble Patch","Promise Commons","Kindling Lane","Primrose Patch","Hearth Rise","Buttercup Grove","Bluebell Acre","Snowdrop Rise","Sprout Green","Honeybee Acre","Honeybee Green","Cornflower Grove","Clover Way","Wildflower Lane","Buttercup Patch","Beehive Commons","Wildflower Commons","Snowdrop Way","Foxglove Patch","Promise Green","Foxglove Corner","Rainwater Rise","Cornflower Lane","Cornflower Fields","Good Earth Commons","Second Chance","Second Harvest","Second Sunrise","Second Spring","Second Wind","Second Breath","Second Bloom","Second Summer","Second Morning","Second Go","New Morning","New Leaf","New Clover","New Bluebell","New Hearth","New Orchard","New Shoots","New Furrow","Fresh Start","Common Ground","Better Days","Still Standing","Start Again","Welcome Home","Green Shoots","Seedtime","Homeward","Brighter Days","Kettle On","Mended Bridge","Good Neighbours","Many Hands","Sunny Side","Lend-a-Hand","Bread and Honey","Hope Springs","Fair Weather","Seed and Spade","Make Good","Picking Up","Tomorrow Town","The Long Mend","All Together","Fresh Paint","Stone Soup","Rebuilt","Spring Clean"]},"desc":{"scrap":["built entirely from old cars stacked three high","where every roof is made from a different road sign","whose market trades bolts, batteries and bottle caps","where the mayor's office is an upturned bus","whose wind turbines are made from bicycle wheels","where nothing is ever thrown away, only swapped","whose scrap-pickers know every junkyard for fifty miles","where the church bell is an old fire extinguisher","famous for its tinkers, who can fix anything twice","whose walls are made of fridges and washing machines","where the children race go-karts built from shopping trolleys","whose streets are lined with hubcap lanterns","where the currency is screws, sorted by size","built in the shadow of a great heap of old televisions","whose blacksmith works an anvil made from a railway sleeper","where the fanciest house has a car bonnet for a front door","whose scrap towers sway and clank in the wind","where a junk sculpture of a giant robot guards the gate","whose radio station plays the same six records on repeat","where a lucky find can make you rich by teatime","whose people can build a wind-up radio from almost anything","where the town hall is a shipping container painted bright yellow","whose kettle is always on and always slightly rusty","where traders arrive every Saturday with carts piled high","whose market day ends with a race of homemade carts"],"fortified":["behind walls made of shipping containers stacked four high","whose gates open only at dawn and close at sunset","built inside an old football stadium","where lookouts watch the horizon from the top of a crane","whose walls are patched with car doors and corrugated iron","where every visitor must answer a riddle at the gate","built around a reservoir that never runs dry","whose drawbridge is an old lorry ramp","where the watchtowers are lit by the last working floodlights","whose council of elders meets in the old guardhouse","built on an island in a river, reached by a single bridge","whose walls have never once been breached","where the gatekeeper keeps a ledger of every traveller","built inside the walls of an old prison, with the doors now always open","whose sandbag walls are rebuilt every spring","where the guards ring a bell every hour to say all is well","built on top of a hill with a view for twenty miles","whose wall is painted with the names of everyone who built it","where traders must leave their carts outside the gate","whose greenhouse sits safely at the heart of the compound","built inside a concrete car park, one floor per family","whose people take turns on watch, even the mayor","where a moat of old tyres circles the outer wall","whose great gate was once the door of a bank strongroom","famous for its tall walls and its warm welcome inside them"],"nomad":["a caravan of painted buses that never stays more than a week","whose wagons are pulled by teams of patient oxen","that follows the rain across the plains","whose sand-yachts sail across the dry lakes","that sets up camp on the same motorway bridge every spring","whose tents are sewn from old billboards","led by a navigator who can read the stars","whose children learn to drive before they learn to read","that trades seeds in the spring and salt in the autumn","whose camp circles its wagons every night","that carries its gardens in the back of a lorry","whose storyteller remembers every road they have travelled","that moves on whenever the wind changes","whose kites can be seen for miles before they arrive","that holds a market wherever it stops","whose horses wear bells so they never get lost","that winters in the ruins of an old service station","whose leader is chosen by a race each midsummer","that never takes the same road twice","whose campfire songs are older than the road itself","that keeps a map of every well between here and the coast","whose bicycles pull carts piled high with pots and pans","that welcomes anyone who can carry their own pack","whose camp appears overnight and vanishes by morning","that follows the herds south every winter"],"ruins":["where three hundred people live in what the old city left behind","whose families share the rooms, the roof and the chores","where the old signs still hang, though nobody follows them","whose rooftop gardens can be seen from the motorway","where the market is held on the frozen escalators across the road","whose people climb in through the windows because the doors are rusted shut","where ivy has covered everything but the welcome sign","whose children play hopscotch on the old p